---
import Layout from '~/layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import HeroText from '~/components/widgets/HeroText.astro';
import Content from '~/components/widgets/Content.astro';
import CallToAction from '~/components/widgets/CallToAction.astro';

const metadata = {
  title: "From Documents to Operations -- OKELAS",
  description: "OKELAS started from a basic question: what actually happens between a document existing and a decision getting made correctly? The full sequence: Process to Workflow to Event to Evidence to Knowledge to Decision to Action.",
};
---

<Layout metadata={metadata}>
  <HeroText
    tagline="Why OKELAS"
    title="From Documents to Operations"
  />

  <Content
    
    content={`
      <p>OKELAS didn't start as "let's build an AI chatbot." It started from a more basic, less exciting question: what actually happens between a document existing and a decision getting made correctly?</p>

      <p>Most businesses go through a recognizable sequence, whether they name it or not. Paper becomes Word files and spreadsheets. Spreadsheets get digitized into a shared drive or a basic DMS -- paperless, but not yet organized. Some businesses take the next step into a proper eQMS, where records and approvals are structured. Fewer take the step after that: connecting process, workflow and evidence so that what happened is provably traceable, not just filed. And fewer still reach the final stage, where that structured operational history becomes something a person -- or an AI system -- can query, reason over, and act on.</p>

      <p>Digitalization projects often stop at "paperless" and call it transformation. It isn't. Scanning a form doesn't make the process behind it any more consistent -- it just makes the inconsistency easier to store.</p>

      <p>OKELAS is built around the full sequence: <strong>Process &rarr; Workflow &rarr; Event &rarr; Evidence &rarr; Knowledge &rarr; Decision &rarr; Action.</strong> Each stage only creates value once the one before it is solid. That's also why OKELAS doesn't assume every company should start at the same point -- a business already running a decent eQMS has a different starting point than one still running on shared spreadsheets, and the honest first move is figuring out which stage you're actually at.</p>
    `}
  />

  <CallToAction
    actions={[
      {
        variant: 'primary',
        text: 'Take the Digitalization Readiness Assessment',
        href: '/readiness/digitalization',
        icon: 'tabler:clipboard-check',
      },
    ]}
  >
    <Fragment slot="title">Next</Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="subtitle">
      Find out which stage your operations are actually at.
    </Fragment>
  </CallToAction>
</Layout>
